From e65200bb2301c050c3fb1e5d1cfc37afceb3f715 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rishabh <iea@iitgn.ac.in>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 05:53:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Open the field apps inside PostMan, and stop shipping the
 file twice

The apps open in a panel over the working area now, rather than a pop-up.
A pop-up is three things the engineer has to manage - a blocker to allow, a
window to find again, a window to close - for no gain. In a panel the app
is simply the next screen, and the workbook still arrives the same way:
posted back, decoded, handed to importAny. test/panel.mjs runs PostMan on
one port and a fake app on another, because a same-origin frame would prove
nothing here.

The pop-up is not gone and will not be. Every card keeps "Open in a new
window", and the panel offers it too, because a site can refuse to be
framed and an app that has not been updated can only post to an opener.
test/handoff.mjs now covers that route specifically.

What the panel does NOT do is claim the app loaded. A frame the browser
refused over X-Frame-Options fires `load` as well, on its own error page,
and nothing readable cross-origin tells the two apart - so a 'load' handler
that turns the note green puts a tick over a blank rectangle. The first
version of this did exactly that, and test/panel.mjs caught it by serving
one app with X-Frame-Options DENY. The note now says what is known and
names the way out. An app that posts {kind:'kisem-hello'} on mount is
proof it rendered, and the note upgrades itself; apps that never send one
lose nothing.

Separately: PostMan.html and index.html were byte-identical, both tracked,
1.2 MB each - git carried the whole thing twice on every commit and
build.py wrote it twice on every build. One name now, index.html, the one
Vercel serves. Anyone who wants a local copy saves the page from the
browser; it is the same file and always was. serve.js (the launcher that
was removed from the product a while ago) and PUSH.md (instructions for a
push that has happened) go with it.

README says plainly what a saved local copy cannot do - the field apps
cannot post back and OCR cannot fetch its model, both because a file://
page has no origin - instead of implying the two copies are equivalent.

All eleven suites pass: forms, full, hard, roundtrip, acmp, fox, handoff,
panel, bills, detect, ui.

